{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"alternative_architecture\":{\"description\":\"\",\"needed\":true,\"why_better\":\"The emerging evidence favors collapsing the pipeline around one gameplay delivery loop rather than continuing subsystem-by-subsystem construction.\"},\"architecture_summary\":\"The repository has strong safety primitives but no executable autonomous gameplay path. Its implemented pipeline is already roughly 9,500 Python lines outside Reconciliation, while Reconciliation adds about 15,200 lines; the 37 task contracts add about 3,300 lines. Since 2026-08-20, Git history shows 126 commits touching Pipeline/Docs/Tasks but only two touching Assets, both camera test/scene hardening rather than a new gameplay feature.\",\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"Whether a single real feature run would reveal that the task/evidence rigor pays back its cost, because no repeated feature-delivery evidence exists yet.\",\"confidence\":0.68,\"do_not_build_yet\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"observation\":\"The current schema-v2 CLI deliberately returns no ready work and denies every dispatch.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/taskcontrol.py:180; Pipeline/TaskGraph/execution_authority.py:6\"},{\"observation\":\"Any change anywhere in the canonical GDD makes prior task conformance stale because records bind the hash of the entire GDD, not the governing excerpts.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/TaskGraph/current_conformance.py:166\"},{\"observation\":\"The implemented production GDD RAG explicitly excludes context packs, project scanning, decomposition, artifact authority, supervision, and GER integration.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/GDDRAG/README.md:196\"},{\"observation\":\"History is overwhelmingly pipeline work rather than game advancement after the initial prototype work.\",\"path\":\"git history at frozen commit 9f2485d\"}],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"Whole-document GDD hashing turns an unrelated wording or distant-design edit into revalidation demand for every delivered task with evidence.\"],\"human_intervention_points\":[],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[],\"missing_components\":[\"No task selection/readiness policy\",\"No gameplay ExecutionCrew\",\"No Unity validation orchestration from a task attempt\",\"No branch/worktree delivery coordinator\",\"No merge/completion path\"],\"next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[],\"proof_of_value\":\"\",\"title\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"},\"observed_failure_solutions\":[],\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"overengineering\":[\"Full reconciliation and its verification/refinement machinery is much larger than the playable implementation it is intended to accelerate.\"],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Current handoff state is duplicated and contradictory.\",\"Conformance is a useful derived state but cannot currently feed readiness, leaving the durable graph inert.\"],\"strong_decisions\":[\"Deterministic facts over model claims\",\"One bounded worker before parallelism\",\"Runtime/Unity evidence and human experiential checks\",\"No silent design invention\"],\"structural_flaws\":[\"Milestone progress has optimized infrastructure correctness without establishing a vertical feature-delivery path.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"At the frozen commit, the architecture is not yet capable of material autonomous development leverage: it can retrieve canon, invoke providers, validate graph structure, and inspect one baseline, but cannot choose, implement, validate, integrate, or complete a gameplay task end to end.\",\"verdict_reason\":\"The core safety ideas are sound, but the implemented composition and ordering are not: substantial machinery has accumulated around planning, audit, and provider boundaries while the first autonomous gameplay delivery loop remains absent.\"}"}}
